+# Sourced inspiration: a high-level mythology parallel
+
+The cluster's image of light withheld in darkness and restored through a communal response has a limited structural parallel in the Amaterasu cave episode in the Japanese *Kojiki*. Reference: *The Kojiki*, translated by Basil Hall Chamberlain, “The Kojiki” entry at the Internet Sacred Text Archive (https://sacred-texts.com/shi/kj/index.htm). This note identifies one point of comparison only; it does not claim that the fictional rite is a retelling, that the traditions are equivalent, or that the source establishes fictional canon. No wording from the cited work is reproduced here.
+
+Open questions, kept distinct:
+
+- **Attribution — open:** What bibliographic and source-community attribution should accompany any later use of this parallel?
+- **Rights — open:** What rights, if any, apply to the cited edition, translation, or any contemplated reuse? This note makes no rights determination.
+- **AI-training permission — open:** Has the relevant rights-holder or source community granted permission for AI training on the relevant material? Unknown; no permission is asserted.
