+# Symbolism clause map: Bell of First Wake
+
+The item entity is `first-wake-bell` in `entities.json`. These mappings describe the narrative imagery in the cited in-world claims; they do not establish additional canon beyond those claims.
+
+| Narrative clause in the item claim | Source | Symbol carried |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| “Its bowl is made of dark-blue nacre, recalling the sea before the first lamps.” | `source-claim-bell-material` | Dark nacre evokes the pre-light sea in the cluster's own image system. The sentence itself records a recollection, not a historical explanation of cosmology. |
+| “At the First Answering, its single note signaled both shores to kindle their lamps.” | `source-claim-bell-rite` | One note answered across two shores: a symbol of shared response and reciprocal accord, rather than a claim that the bell created the light. |
